# shell: desktop
# AW-076: the info window's icon stands for what the window is about, so a
# secondary click on it offers that thing's own menu -- and the items work,
# which is why the actions can be carried out against a path rather than a
# window's selection.
wait 6
click-row 1
wait 3
key i ctrl
wait 10
expect-title info
note the icon answers with the menu the pose itself would get
press 148 125 3
wait 2
release 148 125 3
wait 5
expect-menu Open|Edit query|Open with…|Get info|Edit name|Duplicate|Move to Trash||Move to|Copy to|Create link|Cut|Copy|Paste||Identify|Add-ons|
note and choosing one acts on the thing the window is about
menu-pick Duplicate
wait 30
expect-file /tmp/trk_script/a.txt copy
quit
